From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 05:14:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: g16: Optionally check the session once per
 pass

check_hangs opens with transport_error(), which runs Session::check:
the latched failure, the RTKit and ASC state, the pstate register and a
walk of the adopted UAT bindings. A submission's own publish pass has
just run the same check, so it pays for it twice, and a poll pass runs
it four times: its own check and three check_hangs calls, plus one per
trailing poll. g16_pass_check_once removed publish()'s own repeat but
not the one inside check_hangs.

Add g16_check_once (runtime 0644, default 0). With 1, the transport
check at the head of check_hangs reuses the session check that its own
pass already ran and passed, and reads only the latched failure. A pass
holds that verdict in a scope opened by Firmware::poll, or by publish()
when publish runs its own check. A scope that is dropped restores the
verdict that was there before. Every other path checks in full,
including the recovery loop, which keeps calling transport_error()
itself. The recovery, receipt and deadline checks of check_hangs run as
before.

The rule is in a core-only module with host tests. A stats line counts
the full and the reused checks. Nothing changes while the word is 0.

Assisted-by: LLM
